#: ../../../Lexicon.md:11
msgid "**ADCE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:12
msgid "Aggressive Dead Code Elimination"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:14
msgid "**AST**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:15
msgid "Abstract Syntax Tree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:17
msgid ""
"Due to Clang's influence (mostly the fact that parsing and semantic   "
"analysis are so intertwined for C and especially C++), the typical   working "
"definition of AST in the LLVM community is roughly \"the   compiler's first "
"complete symbolic (as opposed to textual)   representation of an input "
"program\".   As such, an \"AST\" might be a more general graph instead of a "
"\"tree\"   (consider the symbolic representation for the type of a typical "
"\"linked   list node\"). This working definition is closer to what some "
"authors   call an \"annotated abstract syntax tree\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:27
msgid "Consult your favorite compiler book or search engine for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:29
msgid "B"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:33
msgid "**BB Vectorization**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:34
msgid "Basic-Block Vectorization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:36
msgid "**BDCE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:37
msgid ""
"Bit-tracking dead code elimination. Some bit-wise instructions (shifts,   "
"ands, ors, etc.) \"kill\" some of their input bits -- that is, they make "
"it   such that those bits can be either zero or one without affecting "
"control or   data flow of a program. The BDCE pass removes instructions that "
"only   compute these dead bits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:43
msgid "**BURS**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:44
msgid ""
"Bottom Up Rewriting System --- A method of instruction selection for code   "
"generation.  An example is the   [BURG](http://www.program-transformation."
"org/Transform/BURG) tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:48
msgid "C"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:50
msgid "**CFI**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:51
msgid ""
"This abbreviation has two meanings.   Either:   Call Frame Information. Used "
"in DWARF debug info and in C++ unwind info   to show how the function "
"prologue lays out the stack frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:56
msgid ""
"Or:   Control Flow Integrity. A general term for computer security "
"techniques   that prevent a wide variety of malware attacks from redirecting "
"the flow   of execution (the control flow) of a program."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:61
msgid "**CIE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:62
msgid ""
"Common Information Entry.  A kind of CFI used to reduce the size of FDEs.   "
"The compiler creates a CIE which contains the information common across "
"all   the FDEs.  Each FDE then points to its CIE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:66
msgid "**CSE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:67
msgid ""
"Common Subexpression Elimination. An optimization that removes common   "
"subexpression computation. For example `(a+b)*(a+b)` has two   "
"subexpressions that are the same: `(a+b)`. This optimization would   perform "
"the addition only once and then perform the multiply (but only if   it's "
"computationally correct/safe)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:73
msgid "D"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:75
msgid "**DAG**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:76
msgid "Directed Acyclic Graph"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:81
msgid "**Derived Pointer**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:82
msgid ""
"A pointer to the interior of an object, such that a garbage collector is   "
"unable to use the pointer for reachability analysis. While a derived "
"pointer   is live, the corresponding object pointer must be kept in a root, "
"otherwise   the collector might free the referenced object. With copying "
"collectors,   derived pointers pose an additional hazard that they may be "
"invalidated at   any {ref}`safe point <safe point>`. This term is used in "
"opposition to   {ref}`object pointer <object pointer>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:90
msgid "**DSA**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:91
msgid "Data Structure Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:93
msgid "**DSE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:94
msgid "Dead Store Elimination"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:96
msgid "E"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:98
msgid "**ento**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:99
msgid ""
"This namespace houses the   [Clang Static Analyzer](https://clang.llvm.org/"
"docs/ClangStaticAnalyzer.html).   It is an abbreviation of [entomology]"
"(https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entomology)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:105
msgid ""
"In the past, this namespace had not only the name `GR` (aka. Graph   "
"Reachability) but also `entoSA`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:108
msgid "F"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:110
msgid "**FCA**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:111
msgid "First Class Aggregate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:113
msgid "**FDE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:114
msgid ""
"Frame Description Entry. A kind of CFI used to describe the stack frame of   "
"one function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:117
msgid "G"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:119
msgid "**GC**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:120
msgid ""
"Garbage Collection. The practice of using reachability analysis instead of   "
"explicit memory management to reclaim unused memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:123
msgid "**GEP**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:124
msgid ""
"`GetElementPtr`. An LLVM IR instruction that is used to get the address   of "
"a subelement of an aggregate data structure. It is documented in detail   "
"[here](https://llvm.org/docs/GetElementPtr.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:128
msgid "**GVN**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:129
msgid ""
"Global Value Numbering. GVN is a pass that partitions values computed by a   "
"function into congruence classes. Values ending up in the same congruence   "
"class are guaranteed to be the same for every execution of the program.   In "
"that respect, congruency is a compile-time approximation of equivalence   of "
"values at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:135
msgid "H"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:139
msgid "**Heap**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:140
msgid ""
"In garbage collection, the region of memory which is managed using   "
"reachability analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:143
msgid "I"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:145
msgid "**ICE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:146
msgid ""
"Internal Compiler Error. This abbreviation is used to describe errors   that "
"occur in LLVM or Clang as they are compiling source code. For example,   if "
"a valid C++ source program were to trigger an assert in Clang when   "
"compiled, that could be referred to as an \"ICE\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:151
msgid "**ICF**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:152
msgid "Identical Code Folding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:154
msgid "**ICP**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:155
msgid "Indirect Call Promotion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:157
msgid "**IPA**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:158
msgid ""
"Inter-Procedural Analysis. Refers to any variety of code analysis that   "
"occurs between procedures, functions or compilation units (modules)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:161
msgid "**IPO**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:162
msgid ""
"Inter-Procedural Optimization. Refers to any variety of code optimization   "
"that occurs between procedures, functions or compilation units (modules)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:165
msgid "**ISel**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:166
msgid "Instruction Selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:168
msgid "L"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:170
msgid "**LCSSA**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:171
msgid "Loop-Closed Static Single Assignment Form"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:173
msgid "**LGTM**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:174
msgid ""
"\"Looks Good To Me\". In a review thread, this indicates that the   reviewer "
"thinks that the patch is okay to commit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:177
msgid "**LICM**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:178
msgid "Loop Invariant Code Motion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:180
msgid "**LSDA**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:181
msgid ""
"Language Specific Data Area.  C++ \"zero cost\" unwinding is built on top "
"a   generic unwinding mechanism.  As the unwinder walks each frame, it "
"calls   a \"personality\" function to do language-specific analysis.  Each "
"function's   FDE points to an optional LSDA which is passed to the "
"personality function.   For C++, the LSDA contains info about the type and "
"location of catch   statements in that function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:188
msgid "**Load-VN**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:189
msgid "Load Value Numbering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:191
msgid "**LTO**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:192
msgid "Link-Time Optimization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:194
msgid "M"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:196
msgid "**MC**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:197
msgid "Machine Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:199
msgid "N"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:203
msgid "**NFC**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:204
msgid ""
"\"No functional change\". Used in a commit message to indicate that a "
"patch   is a pure refactoring/cleanup.   Usually used in the first line, so "
"it is visible without opening the   actual commit email."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:209
msgid "O"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:214
msgid "**Object Pointer**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:215
msgid ""
"A pointer to an object such that the garbage collector is able to trace   "
"references contained within the object. This term is used in opposition to   "
"{ref}`derived pointer <derived pointer>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:219
msgid "P"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:221
msgid "**PGO**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:222
msgid "Profile-Guided Optimization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:224
msgid "**PR**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:225
msgid ""
"Problem report. A bug filed on   [the LLVM Bug Tracking System](https://bugs."
"llvm.org/enter_bug.cgi)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:228
msgid "**PRE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:229
msgid "Partial Redundancy Elimination"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:231
msgid "R"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:233
msgid "**RAUW**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:234
msgid ""
"Replace All Uses With. The functions `User::replaceUsesOfWith()`,   `Value::"
"replaceAllUsesWith()`, and   `Constant::replaceUsesOfWithOnConstant()` "
"implement the replacement of one   Value with another by iterating over its "
"def/use chain and fixing up all of   the pointers to point to the new "
"value.  See   also   {ref}`def/use chains <iterate_chains>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:242
msgid "**Reassociation**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:243
msgid ""
"Rearranging associative expressions to promote better redundancy "
"elimination   and other optimizations.  For example, changing `(A+B-A)` into "
"`(B+A-A)`,   permitting it to be optimized into `(B+0)` then `(B)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:247
msgid "**RFC**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:248
msgid ""
"Request for Comment. An email sent to a project mailing list in order to   "
"solicit feedback on a proposed change. See also: the {doc}`RFC process   "
"<RFCProcess>` documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:255
msgid "**Root**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:256
msgid ""
"In garbage collection, a pointer variable lying outside of the   {ref}`heap "
"<heap>` from   which the collector begins its reachability analysis. In the "
"context of code   generation, \"root\" almost always refers to a \"stack "
"root\" --- a local or   temporary variable within an executing function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:262
msgid "**RPO**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:263
msgid "Reverse postorder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:265
msgid "**RTTI**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:266
msgid "Run-time Type Information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:268
msgid "S"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:272
msgid "**Safe Point**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:273
msgid ""
"In garbage collection, it is necessary to identify   {ref}`stack roots "
"<stack roots>` so that   reachability analysis may proceed. It may be "
"infeasible to provide this   information for every instruction, so instead "
"the information is   calculated only at designated safe points. With a "
"copying collector,   {ref}`derived pointers <derived pointers>` must not be "
"retained across safe   points and {ref}`object pointers <object pointers>` "
"must be reloaded from   stack roots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:282
msgid "**SDISel**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:283
msgid "Selection DAG Instruction Selection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:285
msgid "**SCC**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:286
msgid "Strongly Connected Component"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:288
msgid "**SCCP**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:289
msgid "Sparse Conditional Constant Propagation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:291
msgid "**SLP**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:292
msgid ""
"Superword-Level Parallelism, same as {ref}`Basic-Block Vectorization   "
"<lexicon-bb-vectorization>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:295
msgid "**Splat**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:296
msgid "Splat refers to a vector of identical scalar elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:298
msgid ""
"The term is based on the PowerPC Altivec instructions that provided   this "
"functionality in hardware. For example, \"vsplth\" and the corresponding   "
"software intrinsic \"vec_splat()\". Examples of other hardware names for "
"this   action include \"duplicate\" (ARM) and \"broadcast\" (x86)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:303
msgid "**SRoA**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:304
msgid "Scalar Replacement of Aggregates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:306
msgid "**SSA**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:307
msgid "Static Single Assignment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:309
msgid "**Stack Map**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:310
msgid ""
"In garbage collection, metadata emitted by the code generator which   "
"identifies {ref}`roots <roots>` within the stack frame of an executing   "
"function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:314
msgid "T"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:316
msgid "**TBAA**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:317
msgid "Type-Based Alias Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:320
msgid "W"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:322
msgid "**WPD**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:323
msgid "Whole Program Devirtualization"
msgstr ""
